stants, A management application searching for a  particular  in‐
terface  should  start  with row 1 and continue through the table
row‐by‐row until the desired interface is found, or the interface
count is reached.  Note that the table may  be  sparse,  i.e.,  a
given  row may not exist, indicated by an of Such an error should
be ignored, and the next row should be checked.  The generic  in‐
terface  information,  common  to all interfaces, can be accessed
